## Wrist splints

Wearing a **wrist splint at night** keeps your wrist straight and takes pressure off the nerve. You may need to wear it for several weeks to see a difference. A pharmacist, GP or physiotherapist can advise.

## Changing how you use your hands

- take regular breaks from repetitive tasks
- avoid bending your wrist for long periods
- use tools with bigger grips, and reduce vibration where you can

## Steroid injections

A **steroid injection** into the wrist can reduce swelling and ease symptoms. The effect may wear off after some months.

## Surgery

If symptoms are severe, or do not get better, you may be offered **carpal tunnel release**. The surgeon cuts a ligament in the wrist to make more space for the nerve.

- it is usually done under **local anaesthetic** as a day case
- most people have good results
- you should avoid heavy lifting for a few weeks afterwards

Do not wait too long if you have constant numbness or weakness, as the nerve can be permanently damaged.
